# Screens: the mouse and the laser share a menu's cursor (LINUX_TESTS.md, "Mouse in VR menus"). The mouse takes the cursor
# when it moves; the right hand's laser takes it when its trigger is pulled on the menu and keeps it; the mouse takes it
# back, going on from where the laser left it.

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: nothing built. A menu is opened with the keyboard by the harness (the inventory, I), because
# ---- the file tests who holds its cursor, not how it is opened.

log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
# The right hand rests below the menu, aimed down.
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.3
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
key I
wait 2
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
# The inventory stands in the world ahead of the eyes, level, at the menu distance.
expect log Menu opened; panel placed within 5
# The right hand at eye height before the face, aimed straight ahead: its laser meets the panel near its middle.
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 0 0
wait 1
expect log Laser: pointing at the panel within 5

# ---- The mouse moves: it has the cursor -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Before: nothing has said the mouse holds the cursor.
expect no log Laser: the mouse moved
mouse 500 300
wait 1
expect log Laser: the mouse moved, so the mouse has the cursor within 5
read cursor
expect result contains MyGuiControl

# ---- The hand moves without pressing: the mouse keeps the cursor ----------------------------------------------------------

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
hand right 0.1 1.55 -0.2 0 0
wait 1
expect no log Laser: a press on the panel

# ---- The trigger on the menu: the laser takes the cursor and clicks there --------------------------------------------------

press right trigger
wait 0.3
release right trigger
wait 1
expect log Laser: a press on the panel, so the laser has the cursor within 5
expect log Laser: left button down at within 5

# ---- The mouse moves again: it goes on from where the laser was, with no jump -------------------------------------------

mouse 520 310
wait 1
expect log Laser: the mouse goes on from the laser within 5
expect no log Exception

key Escape
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
